  "summaries": [
    {
      "block": "library/10665-69096/blocks/prose-sec-000",
      "source": "sections/sec-000-glossary.md",
      "source_hash": "ed81d25c84a114a8c6c42afab85e52316baa3827dd575a7ab6a10e3749d87607",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "A glossary of acronyms used in the PQS guideline, such as AD syringe, GHTF, GMP and ISO, followed by the start of the introduction. The introduction explains that the guideline tells manufacturers how to apply to WHO for pre-qualification of single-use injection devices and how to keep or lose that status.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-69096/blocks/prose-sec-001",
      "source": "sections/sec-001-20-background.md",
      "source_hash": "4420941b0a6d38ddf5f7033925b1215883462c5f9ec2deae34282d2d18aa8cc0",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains why WHO recommends single-use injection devices, including auto-disable syringes, for infection control, and recalls the joint UNFPA, UNICEF and WHO statement that only auto-disable syringes should be used for immunization from 2003. It describes the roles of UN agencies and the medical device industry in securing a reliable supply.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-69096/blocks/prose-sec-003",
      "source": "sections/sec-003-31-what-is-the-pqs-system.md",
      "source_hash": "23c979f2524b887b3c5b46ecc8cd85eae0224a7260ed7f353cd0db7d100cac77",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes the PQS system's origins in the WHO/UNICEF Product Information Sheets, used since 1979 to specify and test immunization equipment. It explains that conforming products will be listed as pre-qualified in an online database and catalogue.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-69096/blocks/prose-sec-004",
      "source": "sections/sec-004-32-transitional-arrangements-for-syringes-for-fi.md",
      "source_hash": "6bba503c5935882777946917252f554de4e53221239ebbb0df2396304558c85d",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains transitional arrangements: from 30 June 2005 UN agencies will in principle buy only devices pre-qualified under the new procedure, with auto-disable and reuse-prevention syringes required to meet the relevant ISO 7886 standards.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-69096/blocks/prose-sec-005",
      "source": "sections/sec-005-33-pre-qualification-of-syringes-for-general-pur.md",
      "source_hash": "0709032f90683f7b3ff2068b88c3399203611d4007c8109e525784c4b3865d1f",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "States that only auto-disable and reuse-prevention syringes will be pre-qualified at first, with therapeutic and insulin devices to be considered in July 2006.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-69096/blocks/prose-sec-006",
      "source": "sections/sec-006-34-what-does-pqs-pre-qualification-mean.md",
      "source_hash": "8b5b6b65821f3a5cd250a7cdf9ff59387e6555d2c11cdc75d948d5e15a7658f5",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains what pre-qualification means: it shows a device is technically suitable for UN procurement but does not guarantee purchase. Purchasers may add their own specifications, which must not conflict with ISO standards.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-69096/blocks/prose-sec-007",
      "source": "sections/sec-007-35-what-products-are-eligible-for-pre-qualificat.md",
      "source_hash": "31022a991caed19ecada1b6a3fd9e518529f433223c7c6fb3c0172bd9fa9efa6",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Defines which syringes are eligible for pre-qualification, requiring compliance with specific ISO standards for therapeutic, fixed-dose immunization and insulin syringes. It notes that needles are not yet covered as a separate category.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-69096/blocks/prose-sec-008",
      "source": "sections/sec-008-36-what-are-the-minimum-licensing-requirements.md",
      "source_hash": "8b04071c8f1d54c772675f977c262daf11e6174be9b50704bbfa7725e8e4aac7",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Sets out minimum licensing requirements: devices licensed in a founding member of the Global Harmonization Task Force meet the quality criteria, while others must show conformity with listed quality system standards. Evidence must come from an accredited certification body as certified copies.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-69096/blocks/prose-sec-009",
      "source": "sections/sec-009-37-how-do-i-apply-for-pre-qualification.md",
      "source_hash": "9995c0532ac1f5012cc579627d7bd0fd9ed6ade718679a9f0de63ea9d8703345",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains how to apply for pre-qualification by sending an introductory letter to the PQS Secretariat describing devices, standards and licensing, with 20 samples per device and site. WHO then either invites a formal application or advises that a device is unsuitable.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-69096/blocks/prose-sec-010",
      "source": "sections/sec-010-38-how-do-i-prepare-a-product-dossier.md",
      "source_hash": "51c230e7cc09e8ddac6a329d90145f4b07786be141d831ed1ea3ea334622496f",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Explains how to prepare a product dossier, requiring a separate dossier for each device type, syringe volume and manufacturing site. It lists the required contents and the address for submission.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-69096/blocks/prose-sec-011",
      "source": "sections/sec-011-39-how-much-will-i-pay.md",
      "source_hash": "042c71067eb589576b127e8a46b6aa203e9c90cfe1458e3a735b0602fc5a0181",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Sets out cost-recovery fees for 2005: US$ 1000 for dossier examination and US$ 700 for each annual re-evaluation, charged per device.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
